      "text": "Let the number be $5\\,41G\\,507\\,2H6.$\nAssume that $5\\,41G\\,507\\,2H6=72n$ for some positive integer $n.$\nSubstituting $5\\,41G\\,507\\,2H6$ for $n,$ we have\n\\begin{align*}\n5\\,41G\\,507\\,2H6 &= 72n \\\\\n\\Rightarrow\\qquad 5\\,41G\\,507\\,2H6 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{72}.\n\\end{align*}Now, we know that $72=8\\cdot 9=9886,$ so, there are $8$ cases that might work.\n\nIf $G=0,01,34,57,$ then $H=6,1,4,7,$ respectively.\nIf $G=2,5,8,$ then $H=0,$ which contradicts $H$ being a single digit.\nPutting all the $8$ of these cases together,\nand using the method of rational roots, we know that the possible values of $GH$ are $0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7.$ The sum of these values is $\\boxed{28}.$. The answer is 28",
